  { id:"PHY12-Q100", board:"CBSE", klass:"12", subject:"PHY12", chapter:2, topic:"PHY12-2-11", type:"short", diff:"hard",
    q:{en:"Explain in one or two sentences why the energy stored in a capacitor includes a factor of ½, rather than simply being charge times final voltage (QV).", hi:"एक-दो वाक्यों में समझाइए क्यों capacitor में जमा ऊर्जा में ½ का कारक शामिल है, बस charge गुणा अंतिम voltage (QV) होने के बजाय।"},
    correct:"potential difference rises from 0 to V during charging so average potential is V/2, giving work = average V times Q|the voltage isn't constant during charging, average is half the final value", exp:{en:"During charging, the potential difference isn't constant at its final value V — it climbs gradually from 0 up to V, so the average potential during the whole process is V/2, and total work = average potential × total charge = ½QV.", hi:"Charging के दौरान, potential difference अपने अंतिम मान V पर स्थिर नहीं है — यह धीरे-धीरे 0 से V तक चढ़ता है, तो पूरी प्रक्रिया के दौरान औसत potential V/2 है, और कुल काम = औसत potential × कुल charge = ½QV।"},
    tags:["theory","hots"], source:"SelfLearn Physics Class 12 Ch2, NCERT-aligned", status:"published" }
